<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul forex market closed for national holiday.</title>
<headline>Seoul forex market closed for national holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Korean foreign exchange market is closed on Thursday, a national holiday, and will reopen on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The won ended Wednesday at 821.00 after opening at 820.70.</p>
<p>Dealers forecast the dollar would trade in a range of 819.50 and 822.00 won on Friday.</p>
<p>Friday's mid-rate is expected to be pegged at 820.90 against Wednesday's 821.80.</p>
<p>-- SHIM SUNG-WON (822) 727 5649</p>
